 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "The $L^2$-weight shifts by one under the Fourier transform",
 "statement": "Let $\\mathcal F$ be a Weil complex on $\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}$ and let\n$\\mathcal G=\\operatorname{FT}_\\psi(\\mathcal F)$. Then, in the\n$L^2$-weight parameter $\\|\\cdot\\|$ of\n[def-wf-l2-norm],\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathcal G\\|\\;=\\;\\|\\mathcal F\\|+1.\n$$",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-a1/sk-p-dl-a1-fourier-weight/lem-fd-l2-plancherel-shift.md",
  "place": "node lem-fd-l2-plancherel-shift, order 2778"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-wf-l2-norm"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By the Plancherel identity of [cor-fd-plancherel] the sums of\nsquares of the trace functions satisfy\n\n$$\n\\|f_{\\mathcal G}\\|_m^2=q^m\\|f_{\\mathcal F}\\|_m^2\n$$\n\nfor every $m$; substituting into the defining ratio of\n[def-wf-l2-norm] shows that the limit superior is positive for a\nparameter $\\beta$ exactly when it is positive for\n$\\beta-1$: the two $L^2$-weights satisfy\n$\\|\\mathcal G\\|=\\|\\mathcal F\\|+1$.",
   "uses": [
    "cor-fd-plancherel",
    "def-wf-l2-norm"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
